 "verdict": "SCREENED - the drive exists, the lever is real only without the drive's metal. A phased RSSR rod (O3 Ti, 2 M2 ball links) turns K 65-77 deg with every pressure angle <= 42 (one-sided cams cap at 46.5 nose / 51.8 roller). Claim s65n2d (committed before its frozen number): frozen exact Bench(110,360) 21.27 (score 92.27), held out 26.19, vs slipper-nose 18.49 / 23.45; complexity 30.5 vs 22.25. No search uses the stroke at the lobe law the CMA picks (K used 42-49). With the hub-2 lobe law at its PA-42 limit (kK 3.0) and the drive metal DELETED (attribution only) the long-dyad chain measures 18.25 / 21.11 (held 2.34 better than slipper-nose); through the real rod drive the same law is 25.83 and its own re-search (cma5) 23.31 / 27.67: the rod drive's crank and ball links do not park (in band 0.5-0.65).",
 "limiter": "Two walls after the stroke. (1) The K LAW: along a q2-driven lobe law th rises ~1.9 deg per q2 degree while a1e rises 1.5 -> 0.9, so the 5 deg margin is lost at th ~109 (kK 2) / ~114 (kK 3.0, the lobe's PA-42 limit); the chain uses ~52-54 deg of K at most, not 75. (2) The DRIVE METAL: the bell crank stacks over link 1b through its 30-55 deg swing (median ~14 mm, in band 0.5-0.6), the ball links sit at 0.55-0.65 and the horn / rod make the contacts (max depth 12.8-14.7 mm); the claim also parks the horn ball 0.25 mm from its ROD-hubK 1 mm pair (r_h +0.25 is the robust build, identical).",
 "note": "Model docs/concepts/models/longstroke-slipper-knuckle-3r.py (LS_DRIVE nose|roller|rssr; LS_STROKE_MIN, LS_OBJ, LS_GHOST for the searches / attribution). Control: slipper-nose verified config through this model at every PA <= 42 = 18.49 frozen (identical: the 42 rule does not bind there). Research note docs/research/longstroke_drive.md.",
 "doc": "docs/concepts/longstroke-slipper-knuckle-3r.md",
